1
00:00:01,839 --> 00:00:06,318
Chapter 68. The blanket.

2
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:11,518
I have given no small attention to that not unvexed subject, the skin of the

3
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:16,638
whale. I have had controversies about it with experienced whaleman afloat and

4
00:00:16,639 --> 00:00:24,558
learned naturalists assure. My original opinion remains unchanged, but it is only an opinion.

5
00:00:24,559 --> 00:00:30,638
The question is, what and where is the skin of the whale? Already you know what

6
00:00:30,639 --> 00:00:35,359
his blubber is. That blubber is something of the consistence of firm,

7
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:41,518
close grained beef, but tougher, more elastic, and compact, and ranges from 8

8
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:45,679
or 10 to 12 and 15 in in thickness.

9
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:50,159
Now, however preposterous it may at first seem to talk of any creature's

10
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:54,719
skin as being of that sort of consistence and thickness, yet in point

11
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:59,679
of fact, these are no arguments against such a presumption, because you cannot

12
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:05,274
raise any other dense enveloping layer from the whale's body but that same

13
00:01:05,275 --> 00:01:10,479
blubber, and the outermost enveloping layer of any animal, if reasonably

14
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:13,999
dense, what can that be but the skin?

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,999
True, from the unmarred dead body of the whale, you may scrape off with your hand

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,999
an infinitely thin transparent substance somewhat resembling the thinnest shreds

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,238
of eisen glass, only it is almost as flexible and soft as satin, that is

18
00:01:32,239 --> 00:01:37,039
previous to being dried when it not only contracts and thickens, but becomes

19
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:42,719
rather hard and brittle. I have several such dried bits which I use for marks in

20
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:48,479
my whale books. It is transparent, as I said before, and being laid upon the

21
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:53,198
printed page, I have sometimes pleased myself with fancying it exerted a

22
00:01:53,199 --> 00:01:58,479
magnifying influence. At any rate, it is pleasant to read about whales through

23
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,198
their own spectacles, as you may say.

24
00:02:01,199 --> 00:02:03,999
But what I am driving at here is this.

25
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,914
The same infinitely thin eisenglass substance which I admit invests the

26
00:02:09,915 --> 00:02:14,878
entire body of the whale is not so much to be regarded as the skin of the

27
00:02:14,879 --> 00:02:20,238
creature as the skin of the skin so to speak. For it were simply ridiculous to

28
00:02:20,239 --> 00:02:24,638
say that the proper skin of the tremendous whale is thinner and more

29
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:27,679
tender than the skin of a newborn child.

30
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:33,274
But no more of this. Assuming the blubber to be the skin of the whale,

31
00:02:33,275 --> 00:02:38,954
then when this skin, as in the case of a very large sperm whale, will yield the

32
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:45,115
bulk of 100 barrels of oil, and when it is considered that in quantity, or

33
00:02:45,116 --> 00:02:50,638
rather weight, that oil in its express state is only three4s, and not the

34
00:02:50,639 --> 00:02:56,159
entire substance of the coat. Some idea may hence be had of the enormousness of

35
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:02,318
that animated mass, a mere part of whose mere integument yields such a lake of

36
00:03:02,319 --> 00:03:08,238
liquid as that. Reckoning 10 barrels to the ton, you have 10 tons for the net

37
00:03:08,239 --> 00:03:13,435
weight of only 3/4 of the stuff of the whale's skin.

38
00:03:13,436 --> 00:03:18,238
In life, the visible surface of the sperm whale is not the least among the

39
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:23,838
many marvels he presents. Almost invariably, it is all over, obliquely

40
00:03:23,839 --> 00:03:28,399
crossed and recrossed, with numberless straight marks and thick array,

41
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:33,518
something like those in the finest Italian line engravings. But these marks

42
00:03:33,519 --> 00:03:38,799
do not seem to be impressed upon the eisenlass substance above mentioned, but

43
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:44,479
seem to be seen through it, as if they were engraved upon the body itself. Nor

44
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:50,558
is this all, in some instances, to the quick observant eye, those linear marks,

45
00:03:50,559 --> 00:03:56,638
as in a veritable engraving, but afford the ground for far other delineations.

46
00:03:56,639 --> 00:04:02,159
These are hieroglyphical, that is, if you call those mysterious ciphers on the

47
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:07,115
walls of the pyramids hieroglyphics, then that is the proper word to use in

48
00:04:07,116 --> 00:04:12,479
the present connection. By my retentive memory of the hieroglyphics upon one

49
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:17,594
sperm whale in particular, I was much struck with a plate representing the old

50
00:04:17,595 --> 00:04:22,799
Indian characters chiseled on the famous hieroglyphic palisades on the banks of

51
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:28,719
the upper Mississippi. Like those mystic rocks too, the mystic marked whale

52
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,799
remains undecipherable.

53
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:35,755
This allusion to the Indian rocks reminds me of another thing. Besides all

54
00:04:35,756 --> 00:04:40,878
the other phenomena which the exterior of the sperm whale presents, he not

55
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:46,238
seldom displays the back, and more especially his flanks, if faced in great

56
00:04:46,239 --> 00:04:51,914
part of the regular linear appearance, by reason of numerous rude scratches,

57
00:04:51,915 --> 00:04:57,039
altogether of an irregular random aspect. I should say that those New

58
00:04:57,040 --> 00:05:01,755
England rocks on the sea coast, which Agassi imagines to bear the marks of

59
00:05:01,756 --> 00:05:06,799
violent scraping contact with vast floating icebergs, I should say that

60
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:11,838
those rocks must not a little resemble the sperm whale in this particular. It

61
00:05:11,839 --> 00:05:16,878
also seems to me that such scratches in the whale are probably made by hostile

62
00:05:16,879 --> 00:05:21,115
contact with other whales, for I have most remarked them in the large

63
00:05:21,116 --> 00:05:24,558
full-grown bulls of the species.

64
00:05:24,559 --> 00:05:28,719
A word or two more concerning this matter of the skin or blubber of the

65
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:34,159
whale. It has already been said that it is stripped from him in long pieces

66
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:39,359
called blanket pieces. Like most sea terms, this one is very happy and

67
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:44,719
significant, for the whale is indeed wrapped up in his blubber, as in a real

68
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:49,679
blanket or counterpane, or as still better, an Indian poncho slipped over

69
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:55,274
his head and skirting his extremity. It is by reason of this cozy blanketing of

70
00:05:55,275 --> 00:05:59,359
his body that the whale is unable to keep himself comfortable in all

71
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:03,359
weathers, in all seas, times, and tides.

72
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:08,558
What would become of a Greenland whale, say, in those shuddering icy seas of the

73
00:06:08,559 --> 00:06:12,878
north, if unsupplied with his cozy cert?

74
00:06:12,879 --> 00:06:18,079
True, other fish are found exceedingly brisk in those hyperboran waters, but

75
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:22,878
these, be it observed, are your coldblooded, lungless fish, whose very

76
00:06:22,879 --> 00:06:27,594
bellies are refrigerators, creatures that warm themselves under the lee of an

77
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:33,274
iceberg, as a traveler in winter would bask before an inn fire. Whereas, like

78
00:06:33,275 --> 00:06:39,359
man, the whale has lungs and warm blood, freeze his blood, and he dies. How

79
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:44,558
wonderful it is, then, except after explanation, that this great monster, to

80
00:06:44,559 --> 00:06:49,359
whom corporeal warmth is as indispensable as it is to man, how

81
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:53,999
wonderful that he should be found at home, immersed to his lips for life in

82
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:59,755
those Arctic waters, where, when semen fall overboard, they are sometimes found

83
00:06:59,756 --> 00:07:05,359
months afterward, perpendicularly frozen into the hearts of fields of ice, as a

84
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:10,799
fly is found glued in amber. But more surprising it is to know, as has been

85
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:15,914
proved by experiment, that the blood of a polar whale is warmer than that of a

86
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:19,518
Borneo negro in summer.

87
00:07:19,519 --> 00:07:25,274
It does seem to me that herein we see the rare virtue of a strong individual

88
00:07:25,275 --> 00:07:33,198
vitality, and the rare virtue of thick walls, and the rare virtue of interior spaciousness.

89
00:07:33,199 --> 00:07:40,079
Oh man, admire and model thyself after the whale. Do thou too remain warm among

90
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:46,079
ice. Do thou too live in this world without being of it. Be cool at the

91
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:52,079
equator. Keep thy blood fluid at the pole. Like the great dome of St. Peter's

92
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:59,594
and like the great whale, retain, oh man, in all seasons a temperature of thine own.

93
00:07:59,595 --> 00:08:05,999
But how easy and how hopeless to teach these fine things. Of erections, how few

94
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:14,116
are domed like St. Peters. Of creatures, how few vast as the whale.
